  <ferc:GeneralDescriptionOfConstructionOverheadTextBlock id="Tag627" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style="text-decoration: underline;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CONSTRUCTION OVERHEAD (UNICAP)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Empire Pipeline, Inc. does not have any employees, however, it receives a percentage of Supply Corporation's UNICAP pool, as a result of borrowing Supply Corporation labor, on a monthly basis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style="text-decoration: underline;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ALLOWANCE FOR FUNDS USED DURING CONSTRUCTION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All construction projects considered to be in progress during the month of which the interest is being computed qualify for AFUDC with the following exceptions:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol style="list-style-type: lower-alpha;"&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Blanket Projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintenance and General Order Projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Production Orders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Voided Projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reimbursable Projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Projects less than 30 days duration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold Projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retirement Projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A project is said to be started in the first month in which it receives charges.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A project is said to be completed in the month in which the asset goes into service.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AFUDC is compounded on a semiannual basis in March and September.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A half-month convention is used for current monthly charges.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:GeneralDescriptionOfConstructionOverheadTextBlock>
