  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="Tag1774" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;!--?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="no"?--&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div class="Section_1"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: center; line-height: 120%; font-size: 10pt; -aw-outline-level: 1;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="text-decoration: underline;"&gt;NATIONAL FUEL EMPIRE PIPELINE, INC&lt;/font&gt;.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: center; line-height: 120%; font-size: 10pt; -aw-outline-level: 1;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: center; line-height: 120%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; text-decoration: underline; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;NOTES TO FINANCIAL STATEMENTS&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: center; line-height: 120%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: center; line-height: 120%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; text-decoration: underline; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;YEARS ENDED DECEMBER 31, 2025 AND 2024&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: center; line-height: 120%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: center; line-height: 120%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; line-height: 120%; font-size: 10pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'upperRoman'; -aw-list-number-values: '1'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 12.17pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;I.&lt;font style="width: 12.17pt; font-variant: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-weight: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;NOTES APPLICABLE TO MORE THAN ONE FINANCIAL STATEMENT:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 120%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 22.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 120%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;A - Summary of Significant Accounting Policies:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 22.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 120%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 120%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Regulation and Basis of Accounting.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; Empire Pipeline, Inc. (Empire) is a New York corporation subject to regulation by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC). Reference is made to Note J for further discussion of regulatory matters.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 120%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;The financial statements are prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the FERC as set forth in its applicable Uniform System of Accounts (USOA) and published accounting releases. This is a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles generally accepted in the United States (GAAP). The main difference between GAAP and the FERC&amp;#8217;s accounting requirements is related to the presentation of amounts collected through customer rates for future costs of removal for property. The FERC presents this as a component of accumulated depreciation, depletion, and amortization, while GAAP presents this as a regulatory liability.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;The preparation of the financial statements requires management to make estimates and assumptions that affect the reported amounts of assets and liabilities and disclosure of contingent assets and liabilities at the date of the financial statements and the reported amounts of revenue and expenses during the reporting period. Actual results could differ from those estimates.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Property, Plant and Equipment.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; Empire&amp;#8217;s principal assets, consisting primarily of gas plant in service, are recorded at the historical cost when originally devoted to service, as required by the FERC. Such cost includes an Allowance for Funds Used During Construction (AFUDC), which is defined as the net cost of borrowed funds used for construction purposes and a reasonable rate on other funds when so used. The AFUDC amounts reported in the accompanying Statement of Income under Other Income and Deductions and under Interest Charges do not represent current cash income, but such amounts ultimately become part of the investment upon which return is earned and are recovered through depreciation over the service life of the facilities constructed. The rates used in the calculation of AFUDC are determined in accordance with guidelines established by the FERC.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;An impairment charge related to the Northern Access Project, which is discussed in Note E - Fair Value Measurements, was recorded in Account 426.5 by Empire at December 31, 2024. The impairment charge reduced the value of certain assets recorded in Account 107, Account 121 and Account 183.2 on the balance sheet. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;Maintenance and repairs of property and replacements of minor items of property are charged directly to maintenance expense. The original cost of property, plant and equipment retired, and the cost of removal less salvage, are charged to accumulated depreciation.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Depreciation, Depletion and Amortization.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; Depreciation, depletion and amortization are computed by application of the straight-line method, in amounts sufficient to recover costs over the estimated service lives of property in service. The provisions for depreciation, depletion and amortization were equivalent to 2.05% and 2.26% of average depreciable property, plant and equipment for the years ended December 31, 2025 and December 31, 2024, respectively.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Unamortized Loss on Reacquired Debt.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; Costs associated with the reacquisition of debt are deferred and amortized over the remaining life of the issue or the life of the replacement debt in order to match regulatory treatment.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Material and Supplies Inventory.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; Plant material and operating supplies are accounted for using average cost.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Stored Gas Inventory.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; Gas stored underground - current, account 164.1, represents over-collection or under-collection of retained gas quantities which is adjusted annually through fuel retention rates to reflect actual experience.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Income Taxes.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; Empire is included as part of the consolidated federal income tax return filed by National Fuel Gas Company (the Company). The return is filed on the basis of a September 30 year end.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;Empire follows the authoritative guidance for Accounting for Income Taxes. Reference is made to Note D for income tax disclosure.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Asset Retirement Obligations.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; Empire accounts for asset retirement obligations in accordance with the authoritative guidance that requires entities to record the fair value of a liability for an asset retirement obligation in the period in which it is incurred. An asset retirement obligation is defined as a legal obligation associated with the retirement of a tangible long-lived asset in which the timing and/or method of settlement may or may not be conditional on a future event that may or may not be within the control of a company. When the liability is initially recorded, the entity capitalizes the estimated cost of retiring the asset as part of the carrying amount of the related long-lived asset. Over time, the liability is adjusted to its present value each period and the capitalized cost is depreciated over the useful life of the related asset.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;Empire estimates the fair value of its asset retirement obligations based on the discounting of expected cash flows using various estimates, assumptions and judgments regarding certain factors such as the existence of a legal obligation for an asset retirement obligation; estimated amounts and timing of settlements; the credit-adjusted risk-free rate to be used; and inflation rates. Asset retirement obligations incurred in the current period were Level 3 fair value measurements as the inputs used to measure the fair value are unobservable.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;Empire has recorded future asset retirement obligations associated with certain costs connected with the retirement of transmission mains and other components in the pipeline system. Such retirement costs are primarily for the capping and purging of pipe, which are generally abandoned in place when retired, as well as for the clean-up of PCB contamination associated with the removal of certain pipe. Empire has also recorded asset retirement obligation costs related to storage tanks.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;Empire&amp;#8217;s future asset retirement obligations (account 230) amount to $1,144,917 and $1,154,166 at December 31, 2025 and December 31, 2024, respectively. In conjunction with the recording of these retirement obligations, Empire has also recorded reductions to regulatory liabilities (included in account 254) related to the cost of removal component of asset retirement obligations of $974,056 and $897,768 at December 31, 2025 and December 31, 2024, respectively.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
