&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;The fair market value of Empire&amp;#8217;s debt, as presented in the table above, was determined using a discounted cash flow model, which incorporates Empire&amp;#8217;s credit ratings and current market conditions in determining the yield, and subsequently, the fair market value of the debt. The fair value of Empire&amp;#8217;s long-term debt was calculated using observable inputs (U.S. Treasuries or Secured Overnight Financing Rate (SOFR) for the risk-free component and company specific credit spread information - generally obtained from recent trade activity in the Company&amp;#8217;s debt). As such, Empire considers the debt to be Level 2.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;On March 6, 2025, Empire borrowed $25,000,000 from the Company at an interest rate of 5.708%. The note matures on March 15, 2030. On the same date, Empire also borrowed $50,000,000 from the Company at an interest rate of 6.119%. This note matures on March 15, 2035. The proceeds of these debt issuances were used to redeem $75,000,000 of 5.779% notes on March 6, 2025 that were originally scheduled to mature on January 15, 2026. The 5.779% notes were redeemed for $75,702,913, plus accrued interest. The call premium was recorded to Account 189, Unamortized Loss on Reacquired Debt, in March 2025. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'upperRoman'; -aw-list-number-values: '3'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 5.51pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;III.&lt;font style="width: 5.51pt; font-variant: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-weight: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;NOTES APPLICABLE TO STATEMENT OF CASH FLOWS:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 22.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;L - Statement of Cash Flows:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 22.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;For purposes of the Statement of Cash Flows, Empire considers all highly liquid investments with a maturity of generally three months or less to be cash equivalents. Interest paid to the Company for the years ended December 31, 2025 and December 31, 2024 was $10,527,806 and $9,725,500, respectively. Net income taxes paid to the Company for the years ended December 31, 2025 and December 31, 2024 was $7,809,083 and $6,610,594, respectively. Income taxes are paid by the Company on a consolidated basis. Empire pays its share to the Company, if applicable.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;Empire has accounts payable and accrued liabilities recorded on its Balance Sheets that are related to capital expenditures. These amounts represent non-cash investing activities at the balance sheet date. Accordingly, they are excluded from the Statement of Cash Flows when they are recorded as liabilities and included in the Statement of Cash Flows when they are paid in the subsequent period. The following table summarizes Empire&amp;#8217;s non-cash capital expenditures recorded as Accounts Payable and Miscellaneous Current and Accrued Liabilities on the Balance Sheet:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
